 {"id":"CF-076","title":"P3 — a Tier-2 PASS is bound to a commit that cannot contain the graded change: PERF-013's PASS names 4720cdc (no --layers in that tree) and certifies a sub-1.2 s measurement the fix falsifies","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T15:24:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:24:53Z","detail":{"verdict_run_id":"88e945ac","graded_commit":"4720cdcd44231c8da49b061486ae7683b4f449fc","graded_commit_content":"board only: .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl + events.jsonl (the CF-075 filing)","decisive_commit":"e21f2ce790e6d595c3f13c559358e9b7817532fd","decisive_commit_contains":"scripts/project-node.sh 5 x --layers, tests/selftest.sh 7 x --layers, specs/NODE.md 2 x --layers"},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 by the code-factory QA lane (tick code-factory-qa-2026-11-03-15-19-48) against origin/main 8892086.\n\n(1) .gitreins/history/2026-11-03/88e945ac/verdict.json records task PERF-013, passed=true, commit=4720cdcd4423, with one evidence item whose source is `git show 4720cdcd4423` (22477 bytes, the CF-075 board-filing patch). The feature under grade does not exist at that commit: `git show 4720cdc:scripts/project-node.sh | grep -c -- '--layers'` = 0, tests/selftest.sh = 0, specs/NODE.md = 0. The fix is the next commit: e21f2ce has 5 / 7 / 2. Four of the five graded criteria ('accepts --layers 20,40 and rejects an unknown layer', 'a scoped run prints SCOPE and SKIP and never writes node.json', 'fixtures 4/4b/14/15 use --layers', 'unscoped behaviour unchanged') are therefore unsatisfiable at the tree the verdict names.\n\n(2) The tier-2 detail cites text that is not in the graded tree: items[0] = {status: PASS, detail: 'PASS: --layers 20,40 accepted (SCOPE line printed, exit 1 from real FAIL rows); --layers 20,99 -> usage text + exit 2; --layers 20, -> exit 2; --layers \"\" -> exit 2. scripts/project-node.sh:54-80 validation.'}. At 4720cdc, lines 54-80 are the role/disk-floor block and the argument loop has no --layers case at all, so the PASS was written from the commit message rather than read from the tree.\n\n(3) Criterion 5 of the same item ('Measured: selftest user+sys below 1.2 s on three consecutive runs') is false even at the fixed tree: e21f2ce's own message reports 1.63 / 1.56 / 1.55 s user+sys, this lane re-measured 1.54 s CPU (real 1.51, user 0.70, sys 0.84; 34 PASS rows; SELFTEST: PASS at 8892086), and the board kept PERF-013 pending marked 'AC-5 unmet' (d4eec41). A numeric threshold was certified PASS without being measured.\n\n(4) The misbinding is systemic, not a one-off. Of the PASS verdicts recorded under .gitreins/history/2026-11-03/, at least three name a commit whose tree contains none of the graded change: PERF-013 -> 4720cdc (board only), CF-055 -> ddff6bc2 (board only; the adapter-counter fix is bb99a5c), CF-058 -> d15205e (verdict-bundle only; the README fix is 557ac3f). The probe below prints touches_named_path=0 for all three. CF-054 -> d088bc6 (README + selftest) and CF-032 -> 8f1e8c1 (merge) are the counter-examples that show the field CAN carry a commit containing the change.\n\nConsequence: the PASS verdict is the artifact a later lane reads before closing a row. CF-073/CF-074 exist because closures mint unresolvable fingerprints; this is the same disease one layer up — the pointer resolves to a real commit that provably cannot satisfy the criteria it certifies, so a stranger cannot falsify the PASS from the artifact. That contradicts AGENTS.md rule 10 ('the control host decides whether it is true') and docs/traceability-doctrine.md rule 4 (a closing verdict binds to a PUBLISHED commit).\n\nNot established here: whether the judge was launched with --scan-root into the worker's worktree; if it was, the tree may have been right and only the recorded pointer is wrong. Either way the artifact states what it graded and it states a tree without the change, and the repair is identical — record the graded tree explicitly and refuse a PASS that does not contain it.\n\nRe-verified in the same tick, independent of this defect: PERF-013's implementation at 8892086 gives 34 PASS rows and SELFTEST: PASS at 1.54 s CPU with 61/61 rows parse; a live 200 fixture on 127.0.0.1:8767 showed the manifest gate works in both directions (unscoped all-green writes node.json, scoped all-green writes none and prints SKIP layer 90); the unscoped output is byte-identical to 4720cdc's script apart from the live mem row; and three reintroduced defects (layer 00 stops printing FAIL for an unreachable URL, layer 40 misclassifies a missing ref as an access failure, layer 30 reports an absent crier identity as ok) each turned the scoped fixtures red, so the perf refactor did not weaken the gate.","acceptance_criteria":"1. A committed, re-runnable audit script (e.g. scripts/verdict_binding_audit.sh <history-date-dir>) prints one line per PASS verdict under .gitreins/history/<date>/*/verdict.json carrying task_id, run dir, recorded commit, whether that commit resolves in a FRESH clone of origin, and whether `git show --name-only <commit>` touches at least one path the graded row's ch:trace names (or, when the verdict carries a scan_commit, that commit). It exits 1 at origin/main 8892086 naming at least PERF-013/88e945ac, CF-055/c75a3783 and CF-058/9bd93bd8, and exits 0 once every PASS verdict names a commit containing the graded change. Paste both invocations and both exit codes into the evidence artifact.\n\n2. A PASS cannot be written without a graded-tree pointer: the judge path records scan_commit (the HEAD of the tree actually read) and that value resolves in a fresh clone of origin, and closing a row refuses a PASS whose graded pointer does not contain the change. Prove it causally in tests/selftest.sh as its own numbered section: with a fixture verdict bound to a commit lacking the change the section prints FAIL naming the task id, with a correctly bound fixture it prints PASS, and the same section FAILs on the pre-fix tree.\n\n3. PERF-013 stops resting on 88e945ac: either a re-judge at e21f2ce whose verdict names e21f2ce (or its scan_commit), or the row records verdict=none:misbound-88e945ac together with the run id, the reason and the exact re-judge command, and every PERF-013 acceptance criterion is re-runnable by a stranger at the commit the row names.\n\n4. Every evidence pointer this row keeps is repository-resolvable: the 88e945ac bundle is either committed (it is untracked today) or the row cites only committed paths, and `git cat-file -e` / `git ls-tree` succeeds for each cited run dir, commit and artifact in a fresh clone of origin.\n\n5. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS, scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK, the board parses every line with no duplicate ids, and the closing commit is pushed with `git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD` = 0.","probe":"cd /home/kara/code-factory\nfor spec in \"PERF-013:88e945ac:4720cdc:scripts/project-node.sh\" \"CF-055:c75a3783:ddff6bc2:scripts/project-node.sh\" \"CF-058:9bd93bd8:d15205e:README.md\"; do\n  IFS=: read -r id run commit path <<<\"$spec\"\n  v=\".gitreins/history/2026-11-03/$run/verdict.json\"\n  c=$(jq -r .commit \"$v\")\n  printf '%s run=%s passed=%s graded=%s touches_named_path=%s\\n' \\\n    \"$id\" \"$run\" \"$(jq -r .passed \"$v\")\" \"${c:0:8}\" \\\n    \"$(git show --name-only --format= \"$c\" | grep -c -x -- \"$path\")\"\ndone\necho \"layers_in_graded_tree=$(git show 4720cdc:scripts/project-node.sh | grep -c -- '--layers')\"\necho \"layers_in_fix=$(git show e21f2ce:scripts/project-node.sh | grep -c -- '--layers')\"\necho \"row_status_PERF-013=$(jq -r 'select(.id==\"PERF-013\")|.status' .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl)\""}
 {"id":"CF-077","title":"P3 — verify-node.sh reports VERIFY: PASS, and node-create.sh reports NODE CREATED, when the auth probe is inconclusive: every status other than 401/302/403/200 is a WARN that never fails","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T15:32:31Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:32:31Z","detail":{"file":"scripts/verify-node.sh:44-58 (auth_gate and unauth_refused legs) and :66-70 (summary)","consumer":"scripts/node-create.sh:61 — `\"$HERE/verify-node.sh\" ... || bad verify`","measured_arms":"stats 401/403 -> PASS rc 0; stats 404 -> WARN + VERIFY: PASS rc 0; stats 000 -> WARN + VERIFY: PASS rc 0; stats 200 -> FAIL rc 1; /api/status without auth_required -> WARN auth_gate + VERIFY: PASS rc 0","measured_consumer":"node-create.sh rc 0, 'NODE CREATED: fixture-node', only auth evidence 'unauth_refused -> 404'","contradicted_docs":"docs/OPERATIONS.md:82 'Require this test to pass before admitting work. A WARN is not approval to expose the gateway.'; docs/THREAT-MODEL.md:47 and :81 classify this exact shape as a fail-closed gap needing repair","not_duplicate_of":"CF-063 (verify-node usage/--help), CF-072 (the '-> 000000' deformation at verify-node.sh:42,53), CF-071 (install-hermes.sh basic_auth substring grep)"},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 by the code-factory QA lane (tick code-factory-qa-2026-11-03-15-19-48, re-fire) at origin/main cb96da8, with a deterministic stub `curl` and `bunker` on PATH so no live node is needed.\n\n(1) The script's own contract says step 3 is 'the gateway's auth gate is closed (unauthenticated request must be 401/302)' (scripts/verify-node.sh:7-8). The implementation makes that a WARN for every other code: 404 (the protected path does not exist, so nothing was proven), 000 (the request never completed), 500, 418 — all print `WARN unauth_refused` and none increments FAILED (scripts/lib.sh:6-7 defines warn() as pure stdout). The summary then prints `VERIFY: PASS` and exits 0. The auth_gate leg has the same shape: `/api/status` without `auth_required` prints `WARN auth_gate` and the run still exits 0.\n\n(2) Measured arms, stub curl returning the code under test: stats 401 -> `PASS unauth_refused ... -> 401`, rc 0; stats 403 -> PASS, rc 0; stats 404 -> `WARN unauth_refused ... -> 404`, `VERIFY: PASS`, rc 0; stats 000 -> `WARN unauth_refused ... -> 000`, `VERIFY: PASS`, rc 0; stats 200 -> `FAIL unauth_refused ... the node is OPEN to the tailnet`, `VERIFY: FAIL (1)`, rc 1 (the check CAN fail, so this is a fail-open on the middle of its input domain, not a dead check); `/api/status` body without auth_required -> `WARN auth_gate`, `VERIFY: PASS`, rc 0.\n\n(3) The consequence is admission, not cosmetics: scripts/node-create.sh:61 runs verify-node.sh and only turns it into a failure on non-zero exit. With the same stub (stats 404) node-create.sh ends `NODE CREATED: fixture-node`, rc 0, and the only auth evidence anywhere in that output is `WARN unauth_refused — /api/system/stats -> 404`. A control host therefore reports a fleet-usable node whose gateway auth gate was never shown to be closed — the exact failure docs/OPERATIONS.md:82 forbids ('Require this test to pass before admitting work. A WARN is not approval to expose the gateway') and that docs/THREAT-MODEL.md:47 and :81 already describe as a fail-closed gap with a recommendation ('fail installation/verification on any uncertainty').\n\n(4) Nothing tests it: `grep -n verify-node tests/selftest.sh` is empty — no numbered selftest section exercises verify-node.sh at all, so the WARN behaviour can neither go red nor be noticed by the repo's own gate. CF-063 covers usage/--help, CF-072 covers the '-> 000000' status deformation in the same lines, CF-071 covers install-hermes.sh's config substring grep; none of them covers the exit status of an inconclusive auth probe or the consumer that trusts it.\n\n(5) Not established here: behaviour against a real bunker node. The defect is in the control-host decision logic and reproduces from a stub, so a live node would only supply a different inconclusive code (404 on an older gateway build, a TLS/proxy error, a timeout), not a different verdict.\n\nNot filed as a duplicate of the CF-031 guard/board set: this is a runtime admission gate, unrelated to commit gating.","acceptance_criteria":"1. verify-node.sh fails closed on an inconclusive auth probe: when /api/system/stats answers anything other than 401, 302 or 403, the run prints a FAIL naming the measured code and exits non-zero (a timeout/000 must also FAIL, not WARN). Prove it as its own numbered section in tests/selftest.sh using a stub curl on PATH: stats 401 and 403 -> that section prints PASS with rc 0, stats 404, 000 and 500 -> the script exits non-zero and prints FAIL naming the code, and the same section prints FAIL when run against the pre-fix scripts/verify-node.sh (paste both runs and both exit codes into the evidence artifact).\n\n2. The auth_gate body leg fails closed too: /api/status without `auth_required: true` is a FAIL naming what was measured, or it stays a warning only behind an explicit, documented opt-out flag (e.g. --allow-warn auth_gate) whose use is printed in the output and in the VERIFY summary line. A default run over a body without auth_required exits non-zero. Selftest covers both arms.\n\n3. The consumer cannot report success on an unverified probe: scripts/node-create.sh prints NODE CREATED only when verify-node.sh reported every auth leg PASS. Prove with the stub fixture: stats 404 -> node-create.sh prints NODE INCOMPLETE and exits 1; stats 401 -> it prints NODE CREATED and exits 0; both arms are selftest sections and both FAIL on the pre-fix tree.\n\n4. The documented meaning matches the code: docs/OPERATIONS.md (gateway/auth section) and docs/THREAT-MODEL.md items 47/81 state the enforced behaviour with the current line references, and every remaining warn() call site in scripts/ that can precede an admission decision is named there with whether it blocks. The sentence 'A WARN is not approval to expose the gateway' must be true of the shipped script.\n\n5. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS (row count unchanged), scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK, the board parses every line with 62+ unique ids, and the closing commit is pushed with `git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD` = 0.","probe":"cd \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\"\nb=$(mktemp -d)\nprintf '%s\\n' '#!/usr/bin/env bash' 'for a in \"$@\"; do case \"$a\" in *hostname\\ -I*) echo 127.0.0.1; exit 0;; esac; done' 'echo ALIVE fixture' > \"$b/bunker\"\nprintf '%s\\n' '#!/usr/bin/env bash' 'o=\"\"; u=\"\"; while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do case \"$1\" in -o) o=\"$2\"; shift 2;; -*) shift;; *) u=\"$1\"; shift;; esac; done' 'case \"$u\" in */api/system/stats) c=\"${STATS_CODE:-404}\";; *) c=200;; esac' 'if [ -n \"$o\" ] && [ \"$o\" != /dev/null ]; then printf \"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"auth_required\\\":true}\" > \"$o\"; fi' 'printf \"%s\" \"$c\"' > \"$b/curl\"\nchmod +x \"$b/bunker\" \"$b/curl\"\nfor c in 401 403 404 000 200; do\n  out=$(PATH=\"$b:$PATH\" BUNKER_SERVER=fixture STATS_CODE=$c bash scripts/verify-node.sh --agent f --port 10800 2>&1); rc=$?\n  printf 'verify stats=%-3s rc=%s %s | %s\\n' \"$c\" \"$rc\" \\\n    \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -E '^(VERIFY|RESULT):' | tail -1)\" \\\n    \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -E 'auth_gate|unauth_refused' | sed 's/^ *//' | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\ndone\nout=$(PATH=\"$b:$PATH\" BUNKER_SERVER=fixture STATS_CODE=404 bash scripts/node-create.sh --project f --repo git@example.invalid:x/y.git --harness hermes --agent f 2>&1); rc=$?\nprintf 'node-create rc=%s %s | %s\\n' \"$rc\" \\\n  \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -E 'NODE (CREATED|INCOMPLETE)' | tail -1)\" \\\n  \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -o 'stats -> [0-9]*' | tail -1)\""}
 {"id":"CF-078","title":"P3 — node.json omits two identity fields specs/NODE.md requires, takes bus.base from an env var no layer sets, and no shipped adapter can reach the write path that would expose it","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Spec vs writer, measured at code-factory@ac30ceb (2026-11-03). specs/NODE.md:7-16 requires the manifest to carry bus.agent_id and harness.version. scripts/project-node.sh:255-266 writes bus{base} and harness{name,port} only — bus.agent_id and harness.version are absent, so a scheduler target that names the crier agent id (specs/NODE.md:19) has nothing to read. The two values it does write are not measurements: repo.path is built as '/home/'+$USER+'/repo' instead of the path the run actually used, and bus.base is read from CRIER_BASE, which grep -rn CRIER_BASE over *.sh/*.md/*.py returns exactly one hit — that same line — while layer 00 (scripts/project-node.sh:147-160) measures CRIER_URL. A run with CRIER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8799 would therefore record http://crier.example:8767. Nobody sees this because the write path is unreachable with the shipped adapters: on this host hermes --apply fails 'FAIL python — hermes-agent 0.19.0 requires python >=3.11,<3.14; found 3.14.9', opencode --check PASSes but --apply prints 'FAIL apply — refused — the opencode install ladder is unmeasured here', claude-code is 'FAIL binary — absent'; and tests/selftest.sh only ever runs scoped, where layer 90 prints 'SKIP layer 90 (fixture mode: no manifest)'. So no shipped path and no test ever produces node.json, and the one code path that does is a string-built identity record. ch:trace row=CF-078 spec=specs/NODE.md#manifest wave=none:qa-tick-no-manifest test=tests/selftest.sh doc=scripts/project-node.sh prompt=prompts/qa.md evidence=none:row-is-the-evidence witness=none:no-live-node verdict=none:filed-not-judged commit=none memory=none:no-durable-record","acceptance_criteria":"1. A green unscoped --apply writes node.json in which bus.agent_id equals the agent id in $HOME/.node/crier.json, harness.version equals the version the adapter's --check printed, repo.path equals `git -C \"$HOME/repo\" rev-parse --show-toplevel`, and bus.base equals the CRIER_URL the layer-00 reach check measured; no field may be string-concatenated or read from a variable no layer sets. 2. `grep -rn CRIER_BASE` returns zero hits, or a specs/NODE.md line that defines it as the manifest field source and a layer that measures it. 3. A committed transcript (tests/selftest.sh section or docs/audits/) shows the node.json produced by a green run, so the write path is exercised by the gate rather than by inspection. 4. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS.","created_at":"2026-11-03T15:42:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:42:22Z"}
